odebase and found several instances of the `grayscale` utility being applied to images. Removing these will bring immediate color. I\'m also considering a \"Midnight Teal\" palette, with a subtle cool-tinted background and a darker foreground. Specifically, I plan to set `#F7F9FA` as background, `#0B1215` as foreground. I\'ll need to define a new accent color too.\n\n\n**Updating Color Choices**\n\nI\'ve decided on a new color palette, moving from the cool tones. I\'m aiming for warmth, and I\'ll update the CSS variables. My new background is `#FAFAF9` (warm white), foreground `#1C1917` (warm dark gray), muted `#F5F5F4` (warm light gray) and muted foreground `#78716C`. The plan is to change the CSS variables in `globals.css` with these new values.\n\n\n"
