  planner_response {
    response: "I have updated the application to introduce a subtle touch of color while strictly maintaining its professional, high-end Dunamis aesthetic.\n\nHere is what was changed:\n- **Restored Photographic Color**: The `grayscale` CSS filters were removed from all imagery across the application (Hero banners, Projects, Articles, Services). Allowing the natural colors of the photography to show through instantly adds vibrancy and depth to the layout without resorting to loud artificial gradients.\n- **Tinted Neutral Palette**: The pure grayscale palette (stark `#111111` blacks and `#FAFAFA` whites) was shifted to a highly professional **Slate & Deep Navy** palette. The background is now a subtle cool off-white (`#F8FAFC`), and the foreground text is a rich slate-navy (`#0F172A`). This adds a refined, almost imperceptible color foundation that feels much warmer and more premium than pure monochrome.\n- **Consistent Button UI**: The mobile menu CTA button was fixed to use the correct `rounded-none` geometry, maintaining the sharp, architectural design language across all viewports.\n\nThe site is now slightly more lively and colorful, but remains squarely on a professional and premium path."
